    {
      "id": "battery_efficiency-2",
      "source": "battery_efficiency.md",
      "text": "energy before using friction brakes. High speed increases aerodynamic drag. On many routes, a moderate and steady speed is more efficient than repeatedly accelerating and braking. Eco mode usually softens throttle response and reduces unnecessary energy demand. Cabin cooling or heating can create a meaningful auxiliary load. A moderate cabin temperature, such as around 24C in warm conditions, can reduce climate energy use while keeping the driver comfortable.",
