      "id": "charging_strategy-1",
      "source": "charging_strategy.md",
      "text": "# EV Charging Strategy Knowledge Fast charging is useful when the driver needs a quick top-up, but it is not always the best option. If the vehicle can comfortably reach the destination with a healthy range buffer, charging after arrival may reduce time pressure and battery stress. Charging habits matter. Frequent unnecessary fast charging can increase battery stress compared with planned charging. A battery utilization copilot should consider route distance, predicted arrival buffer, next trip length, and driver charging history before recommending fast charging. For daily driving, drivers often benefit from maintaining a reasonable charge",
