      "id": "copilot_responses-1",
      "source": "copilot_responses.md",
      "text": "# EVision Copilot Response Style EVision should explain recommendations in simple and human-like language. It should avoid technical jargon while still being specific enough to be useful. Good responses mention the likely cause, the effect on range, and the action the driver can take. For example: \"Your battery is draining faster because traffic idling and cabin cooling are adding extra load. Hold 42-48 km/h in traffic and set the cabin to 24C to save energy.\" The assistant should be proactive on the car screen. Chat and voice can exist as optional features, but the main",
